okay today I'm going to talk to you  about stem cells we're going to talk  about what stem cells are good look at  stem cells in animals and stem cells in  plants we're gonna look at have a look  at the medical uses of stem cells and  some of the barriers to being able to  use themselves in medicine as well so  first of all stem cells are cells which  are described as being undifferentiated  or unspecialized this just means that  they don't have a specific job yet they  have the ability to become more  potentials become a number of different  types of cell so first of all we're  gonna have a look at what  differentiation means so in our bodies  we have lots and lots of different types  of specialized cell so which could do  different jobs so a stem cell is a cell  which is unspecialized the cell which  currently has no job it can become  different types of cells depending on  what its kind of given instructions to  do within the body so for example it  could become a neuron in order to carry  electrical signals it could become some  cardiac muscle in the heart it could  become a red blood cell or it could for  example become a silly eight itself so  there's lots and lots of different types  of specialized cell in the body and they  all have particular jobs the stem cell  is the undifferentiated unspecialized  version that we get the beginning so one  type of stem cells is called  embryonic stem cells now embryonic stem  cells come from embryos that's the name  of the ball of cells the verr developing  ball of cells that will become a fetus  and then a baby so just after  fertilization we have an embryo and all  of those cells are unspecialized they  have the potential to become any type of  cell in the body so literally anytime  that's one type of stem cell the other  type of stem cells are called adult stem  cells so they're found in the body and  essentially adult stem cells are used in  order to produce a narrow range of cells  to replace damaged cells so adult stem  cells are slightly less useful because  they have a limited they have a limited  kind of different options of what they  can become  whereas embryonic stem cells can become  anything at all they're found for  example adults themselves in the bone  marrow now it's not just animal cells  that have stem cells plants also have  stem cells called Mary stems so the big  clue that stem cells it has the word  stem in it so I just show you where  where these stem cells are fine so if we  imagine I just have a little plant here  there's the plant above the ground and  this is obviously the roots below the  ground so we find Mary stems in the tip  of the root and within the tip of the  shoes so these Mary stems can become any  type of cell any type of plant cell so  there and these this can happen  throughout the lifetime without  throughout the whole lifetime of of the  plant so a type of an example of  specialized cell in a plant could be for  example xylem and phloem which transport  substances around the plant so if these  parts here they're tips the chute and  the tips of the root this is where we  find meristems which are  undifferentiated unspecialized plant  cells so what's the big deal about stem  cells how could they actually be used so  their potential uses are for example in  sick or cell anemia now these this is  when someone's born with a condition  where their red blood cells are  misshapen if they can have adult stem  cells put within their bone marrow those  cells can produce healthy red blood  cells it's just really useful stem cells  in the future could be used for spinal  cord injury  this could be extremely important if  someone has a spinal cord injury they  might well be paralyzed if we could put  an undifferentiated stem cell into their  spinal cord they could develop and grow  neurons develop into neurons which could  replace the damage it could also be used  for heart disease so if part of the  heart has been killed or died because of  disease we could potentially use stem  cells which would develop into cardiac  tissue so there's lots of potential uses  lots of different types of injury  ourselves could be just replaced by  using stem cells so what's the problem  why aren't these just used now so  problems first of all big problem is  ethics because embryonic stem cells come  from embryos which are the ball of cells  that will develop into a fetus and then  a baby so lots of people say that is  it's not right to be able to to use  embryonic stem cells because a lot of  people suggest that it's like taking a  life because that embryo would develop  into a person so there's a lot of  ethical issues around using embryonic  skin stem cells which are the more  useful typist themselves also a big  problem is tumors because if we've  introduced stem cell we want it to  divide it could it's very difficult to  control that division it could just keep  dividing and dividing and dividing and  form a tumor which could cause big big  problems next up is disease if whatever  reason somehow there was a virus within  a stem cell and we've planted it at  someone's body we'd be giving them that  particular disease and the final problem  is rejection if we put a stem cell or  stem cells into someone's body their  body may well recognize it as being  foreign and tried to destroy it the  white blood cells might try and break it  down so the stem cells may well be  rejected so that is  basically the summary sheet that is stem  cells summarized I hope it's been useful  thank you
 

